values ('a7b8c9d0-1e2f-4a72-9b22-3c4d5e6f7a02', 'special-topics-seminar', 'Special Topics Seminar', 'Students frame an advanced seminar through research questions, a defined corpus, and a clear scope; read primary texts, cultural objects, and Spanish-language scholarship with annotation, close reading, and synthesis; apply theoretical frameworks to evidence; situate materials in historical, regional, transatlantic, linguistic, and cultural contexts; locate and integrate scholarly and primary sources; lead discussion in Spanish; and develop a research argument from proposal and annotated bibliography through presentation, workshop, revision, and a final paper in academic Spanish.');

